 This changelog starts at version 2.0.0.  
 Previous history is not included.
 
+## [3.2.0] - Unreleased
+
+Errors in queue-based tasks are no longer swallowed: a run that lost results
+now fails instead of finishing normally.
+
+### Added
+- `fail_on_task_errors` configuration option (default `True`).
+- `TaskFailuresError`, raised by `QueueTaskInitializer.start()` when tasks failed
+  and were discarded.
+- `QueueTaskInitializer.delete_task_queues()` and `is_task_queue()`.
+
+### Changed
+- `start()` raises `TaskFailuresError` after post-processing when any task was
+  discarded (inserting-queue failures, or computing-queue failures after a
+  retry). Set `fail_on_task_errors: False` to only log a warning.
+- `delete_queues` now deletes only the task's own queues (computing,
+  inserting and per-model computing queues) instead of every queue on the
+  broker. `delete_all_queues()` is unchanged.
+
+### Fixed
+- Errors in `post_processing()` were logged and ignored; they are now raised
+  when the pipeline itself succeeded. A pipeline error is never masked by a
+  post-processing error.
+- A computing task that always failed was requeued forever; with
+  `GPUTaskInitializer` (`basic_get` loop) the pipeline never finished. Failed
+  tasks are now retried once and then discarded.
+- Database connections use `client_encoding=utf8`, so clusters created under
+  `LC_ALL=C` (`SQL_ASCII`) no longer fail on non-ASCII text.
+
